NOTES: the routines of src/stuntracefx/object that are not converted, and
where the Enhanced calls were left out.

Nothing in native/stuntracefx/src/object has been run. It compiles; the
race flow that would run it is not finished.

Dead routines
-------------
Proof, for each below: no call or jump to it from the game's code in asm/ or
src/ other than from another routine on this list, its address stored by no
live routine, and no three-byte pointer to it in the ROM (scanned over
assets/cart.dat). Routines the original's unit scripts reach count as dead
when that is all that reaches them. Sign-store entries (the "XSign" and
"YSign" entries of the shard, ring and fan routines) are inner entries no
live pointer names; their logic is in the converted routine.

ROM bytes that happen to spell a pointer to a routine do not make it live.
Those seen: 08:D808 ObjectFallerRecord (inside a run of 08 D8), 09:CE30
LapSignStep1, 09:D030 ObjectWheelStepXSign, 03:D289 ObjectSet39To4Continue,
03:C870 ObjectPointDistanceXZ, 03:D2F0 ObjectChildFindTagY. None has a
caller or setter among the live routines. Should the race ever run one, the
handler table reports it once on stderr.

