Original paths that are not reproduced
--------------------------------------
09:EC2A ObjectSlideGateUpStep, a hit with the fog colour at $7FFF: the
original runs operand bytes as code and ends in ROM data at $CA:E7EC. Here
the frame ends. Direct page $5C and $0DA7 are written by these objects and
read by nothing, so those writes are left out; $1A05 likewise (only the
unreached SlideOutWobble reads it).
Direct page $00 (the rails' colour, the shards' third axis) and $80 (the
burst gate's pitch) are read as 0: no label-addressed store writes other
than 0 to them in the game's code. An indexed store landing there was not
ruled out.
Stray stores to low RAM on paths that need a missing record or an empty
list are skipped, with a comment where each is: ring_spawn, the track
director with no entry, ObjectFree with no next, the sky ball when the spawn
fails, ObjectPlaceAll and GsuRecordWords88 with a count of 0.

